      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "Language -Usage Notes \n1. Era is a past tense form of the verb essere. You willlearn more about this \ntense later. For the time being, learn the following other forms: \n(io) ero \n(lei) era (noi) eravamo \n(voi) eravate \n(loro) erano \n2. The word uno or una is used with an adjective to express the idea of \"a ... \none. H Thus: \nuno decaffeinato a decaffeinated one"
